Dear Linux & Cisco IOS Users,

We've released a new preview version of Telconi Terminal (v08a), now 
with support for Secure Shell (SSH) version 1 protocol. With this 
version, you can securely connect to your networking equipment (provided 
your system image supports SSH also). Alternatively, you can also 
connect through a "proxy" SSH Unix box and then use TELNET again to 
access the router or switch.

Short description:

Telconi Terminal, a network management productivity application for 
Cisco IOS based routers, switches and other devices, helps network 
administrators to accomplish their daily work more efficiently and 
comfortably by complementing the IOS command line interface with a more 
convenient, interactive visual user interface.

Important features include:

	- Configuration, exec and debug sessions
	- interactive full-screen configuration editing and browsing
	- support for the IOS integrated help facility
	- interface status and other displays
 	- access-list editing support

	- Native, multi-platform C/C++ application, no Java
	- Single executable on all platforms, no installation required

Downloads and Information

You can download a preview version using the direct download links below:

	http://www.telconi.com

 Windows	
	http://www.telconi.com/download/telconi08.zip

 MacOS X
	http://www.telconi.com/download/TelconiTerminal08aTP.dmg

 Linux
	http://www.telconi.com/download/telconi-linux08.tgz

 FreeBSD:
	http://www.telconi.com/download/telconi-freebsd08.tgz

 Solaris:
	http://www.telconi.com/download/telconi-sol08.tgz

